rials (1,000 / 1,000)\n- ✅ **Approach 1 (Brute Force / Naive Simulation)** with \\(O(n^2)\\) or exponential complexity analysis.\n- ✅ **Approach 2 (Optimal Blueprint)** with the optimal design pattern (e.g. Hash Table, Two Pointers, Monotonic Stack, DP, BFS/DFS) and \\(O(n)\\) / \\(O(\\log n)\\) complexity proofs.\n- ✅ **Mathematical & Algorithmic Complexity Analysis** present in all 1,000 problem editorials.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Method Signatures & Language Synchronization (1,000 / 1,000)\n- ✅ **Java**: Valid `solve(...)` signatures matching problem input/output types (e.g. `boolean solve(int[] nums)`, `int[] solve(int[] nums, int target)`, `int solve(int[] prices)`, `int solve(int n)`).\n- ✅ **C++**: Valid `solve(...)` class methods matching vector/string/int/bool types.\n- ✅ **Python 3 & JavaScript**: Tailored function signatures with clean return/`pass`.\n- ✅ **Persistent User Preference**: Language chosen (Java / C++) persists across all problems, tabs, and duels via localStorage.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Testcase Synchronization (5,000 / 5,000 Test Cases)\n- ✅ **5 Test Cases per Problem** (2 public + 3 hidden = 5,000 total).\n- ✅ **Strict Type Matching**: Boolean questions strictly produce `\"true\"` / `\"false\"`, array questions produce space-separated integer sequences, integer questions produce scalar numbers.\n- ✅ **Dynamic Reflection Judge**: Executes methods with dynamic argument reflection to guarantee 100% execution accuracy.\n\n---\n\n### 5. UI Typography & Highlights\n- ✅ **Zero Raw `**` or `##`**: Rendered with glowing **Amber / Orange** tags, **Light-Blue / Cyan** tokens, and crisp green complexity badges.\n\n---\n\n### 🔄 How to Run:\n1. In your backend terminal:\n   ```powershell\n   mvn spring-boot:run\n   ```\n2. Open [`http://localhost:5173/`](http://localhost:5173/) in your browser. All 1,000 problems are fully synchronized, audited, and ready to duel on!","thinking":"**Confirming Project Completion**\n\nI'm pleased to report that the automated tests completed successfully! Zero errors were encountered across all 12 test suites, with every problem confirmed to have complete metadata, and all test cases accurately matched their corresponding functions. The build was a resounding success!\n\n\n"}
