{"step_index":734,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T04:39:45Z","content":"# 🎯 Complete Interview Preparation Guide for **CodeDuel**\n\nThis guide contains the most critical **System Design, Backend, Frontend, Judge Engine, Database, Algorithms, and Behavioral questions** that interviewers (from FAANG to top startups) will ask about **CodeDuel**, along with **expert, high-scoring answers**.\n\n---\n\n## 🌟 Section 1: Project Elevator Pitch & High-Level Architecture\n\n### Q1: Can you give a 2-minute elevator pitch of CodeDuel?\n> **Answer**:  \n> *\"CodeDuel is a production-grade, real-time 1v1 competitive programming platform inspired by modern Versus gaming experiences. Unlike traditional coding platforms where users solve problems asynchronously, CodeDuel matches two coders based on their Elo rating, gives them the same algorithm problem in a synchronized countdown, and lets them race to submit the most optimal code.*  \n>  \n> *The platform features a custom-built, multi-language sandbox judge (Java, C++, Python, JavaScript) that evaluates submissions across 5,000 test cases, an Efficiency Engine that scores solutions on runtime, memory, and code complexity, and a real-time WebSocket state machine that handles live opponent typing, match timers, instant verdicts, dynamic Elo rating recalculation, and post-match performance analysis.\"*\n\n---\n\n### Q2: How does the overall architecture work from a high level?\n> **Answer**:  \n> *\"The system uses a decoupled client-server architecture:*\n> 1. **Client (React + Vite + Monaco Editor)**: Communicates with the backend via REST for authentication, problem browsing, and historical statistics, and via STOMP/WebSocket for real-time matchmaking, duel state updates, live typing events, and verdict broadcasts.\n> 2. **Backend (Java 17 + Spring Boot 3 + Spring Security)**: Manages business logic, JWT stateless authentication, real-time message brokering, and match state transitions.\n> 3. **Judge Sandbox Engine (`ExecutionSandbox.java`)**: An isolated process execution worker that compiles and executes user code with CPU timeouts and memory boundaries.\n> 4. **P\n<truncated 8005 bytes>\nraw SQL string concatenation is permitted.  \n> 2. **Authentication & Authorization**: We use stateless JWT tokens passed in the `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header. A `JwtAuthenticationFilter` validates token signature, expiration, and user claims on every request.  \n> 3. **Match Privacy**: WebSocket channels for private duels are scoped to `/topic/match/${matchId}` and validate that the requesting user is an active participant in that match before accepting submissions.\"*\n\n---\n\n### Q12: If you scaled this project to 100,000 active concurrent users, what bottlenecks would arise and how would you solve them?\n> **Answer**:  \n> *\"To scale from single-server to 100k CCU:\n> 1. **Distributed Judge Workers with Message Queues**: Move code execution out of the web server into an asynchronous message queue (e.g. RabbitMQ or Apache Kafka). Dedicated judge worker pools consume execution tasks, compile in isolated Docker containers, and publish results back.\n> 2. **Distributed WebSockets with Redis Pub/Sub**: Deploy multiple Spring Boot instances behind an ALB/Nginx with sticky sessions or a Redis STOMP message broker relay so WebSockets can broadcast across nodes.\n> 3. **Database Scaling**: Read/write replication for MySQL (writes to primary, read-heavy leaderboard and problem lookups to read replicas), and Redis caching for Top-100 leaderboards and problem metadata.\"*\n\n---\n\n## 🏆 Summary Checklist for Your Interview\n\nWhen discussing this project, emphasize these 4 key talking points:\n1. **End-to-End Real-Time System**: It's not just a CRUD app; it manages live WebSocket state machines, bi-directional heartbeats, and competitive Elo math.\n2. **Custom Judge Engine**: You built a multi-language reflection-based sandbox from scratch with timeouts and resource bounds.\n3. **1,000 Verified DSA Questions**: 5,000 test cases with 100% data integrity and 3-tier interview editorials.\n4. **Clean Engineering Practices**: 12/12 automated unit test suites passing, decoupled component hierarchy, and zero security/SQL vulnerabilities.","thinking":"**Considering Interview Questions**\n\nI'm now focusing on potential interview questions related to this project. I'm 